# React UI & Tailwind

## Styling

- Custom Tailwind only. Compose utilities; extract repeated patterns into `components/ui`.
- Colors via CSS variables / theme tokens (`bg-surface`, `bg-chrome`, `text-primary`, `bg-accent`). No scattered hex in components.
- Brand palette: champagne gold accent, charcoal chrome, warm off-white canvas; light + dark via `.dark` class.
- Support light/dark/system theme through `ThemeProvider`. Keep UI readable in both modes.
- Responsive admin: drawer nav below `lg`, fixed sidebar at `lg+`; tables wrap in `overflow-x-auto`; touch targets ~44px.
- Avoid generic AI aesthetics: no purple-glow themes, no noisy gradients, no emoji decoration in product UI.

## Components

- Functional components + hooks. Extract a custom hook when logic is reused or heavy.
- Desktop-optimized but mobile-usable: readable tables, filter bars, clear density.
- Every interactive control needs accessible labels, visible focus, and keyboard-friendly dialogs/menus.
- Cover loading / empty / error states with shared patterns (skeleton, empty copy, retry).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="bg-[#c9a227] text-white">Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD
<Button variant="primary" type="submit">Save</Button>
```

## Structure

- Route screens in `pages/`; presentational pieces in `components/` or colocated widgets if page-specific.
- If a UI pattern appears twice, promote it to `components/ui`.
- Keep files focused; split when a screen becomes hard to scan (roughly 200+ lines of JSX).
